# CSS

- Reuse the existing design language. Do not add a CSS framework.
- Do not refactor design tokens as part of an unrelated feature.
- Use clear, feature-specific class names that do not collide with existing classes.
- Avoid `!important` and selectors so specific they are hard to override.
- New components must work in light and dark themes (`body.dark-theme`) and at mobile widths.
- Avoid horizontal overflow.
- New motion must honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. Prefer `transform` and `opacity`.
- Do not add automatic motion that changes layout.

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .writing-new-badge {
    animation: none;
  }
}
```
